<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">4 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 4 April, from 503 BCE to 1975.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/roman-triumph" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/roman-triumph.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">503 BCE <span class="tih-ago">2,528 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Consul Agrippa Menenius Lanatus celebrates a triumph over the Sabines</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Agrippa Menenius Lanatus, a consul of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a>, celebrated a triumph for his victory over the Sabines, an Italic people of the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apennines">Apennine Mountains</a>. The triumph was a ceremonial procession through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> granted to a victorious general.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-triumph">Roman triumph</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">619 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,407 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pulakeshin II's inscription records his victory over Harsha</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pulakeshin-ii">Pulakeshin II</a>, king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalukya-dynasty">Chalukyas</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badami">Badami</a>, issued the Bijapur-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mumbai">Mumbai</a> grant inscription, which mentions his victory over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harsha">Harsha</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kanauj</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narmada-river">Narmada</a>. The battle therefore took place earlier, probably in the winter of 618–619.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pulakeshin-ii">Pulakeshin II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1081">1081 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">945 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alexios I Komnenos is crowned Byzantine emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Days after his troops took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikephoros-iii-botaneiates">Nikephoros III</a>, Alexios Komnenos was crowned emperor. His dynasty steadied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> for a century, and his appeal to the Pope helped prompt the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexios-i-komnenos">Alexios I Komnenos</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1818">1818 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">208 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US Congress fixes the flag at thirteen stripes</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Flag Act of 1818 set the American flag at thirteen stripes for the original colonies, with a star for every state added on the following 4 July. The rule still governs the flag today.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1841">1841 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">185 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William Henry Harrison dies a month into his presidency</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-henry-harrison">William Henry Harrison</a> died 31 days after taking office, the shortest presidency in US history. His death raised the first test of presidential succession, settled when John Tyler took full office.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1865">1865 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">161 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lincoln walks through the fallen Confederate capital</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-lincoln">Abraham Lincoln</a> toured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richmond-virginia">Richmond, Virginia</a>, two days after its evacuation, greeted by crowds of newly freed Black residents. He sat briefly at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jefferson-davis">Jefferson Davis</a>'s desk in the Confederate White House.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1949">1949 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">77 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Twelve nations sign the North Atlantic Treaty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Foreign ministers meeting in Washington signed the treaty that created <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a>, committing members to treat an attack on one as an attack on all. The alliance anchored Western defence through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1968">1968 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">58 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Martin Luther King Jr. is assassinated in Memphis</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther-king-jr">Martin Luther King Jr.</a> was shot dead on the balcony of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a> Motel, where he had come to support striking sanitation workers. Riots broke out in more than a hundred American cities.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1975">1975 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">51 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bill Gates and Paul Allen found Microsoft</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Gates and Allen formed a partnership in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonso-de-albuquerque">Albuquerque</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-mexico">New Mexico</a>, to sell a BASIC interpreter for the Altair 8800. Their company went on to dominate personal computer software.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 4 April <span class="n">2</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ambrosius-blarer"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ambrosius-blarer.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ambrosius Blarer</span><span class="tp">1492–1564</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/maria-ii-of-portugal"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/maria-ii-of-portugal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Maria II of Portugal</span><span class="tp">1819–1853</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 4 April <span class="n">10</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ambrose"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ambrose.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ambrose</span><span class="tp">c. 339–397</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/isidore-of-seville"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/isidore-of-seville.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Isidore of Seville</span><span class="tp">c. 560–636</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-x-of-castile"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alfonso-x-of-castile.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alfonso X of Castile</span><span class="tp">1221–1284</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii-of-denmark"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-ii-of-denmark.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Frederick II of Denmark</span><span class="tp">1534–1588</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/oliver-goldsmith"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/oliver-goldsmith.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Oliver Goldsmith</span><span class="tp">1728–1774</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/andre-massena"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/andre-massena.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">André Masséna</span><span class="tp">1758–1817</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-henry-harrison"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-henry-harrison.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William Henry Harrison</span><span class="tp">1773–1841</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/carol-ii-of-romania"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/carol-ii-of-romania.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Carol II of Romania</span><span class="tp">1893–1953</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther-king-jr"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/martin-luther-king-jr.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Martin Luther King Jr.</span><span class="tp">1929–1968</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/max-frisch"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/max-frisch.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Max Frisch</span><span class="tp">1911–1991</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
